  "instance_name": "mapping_1",
  "label": "The arrival of American forces at Auschwitz is mapped onto the visual of Nazi leaders",
  "description": "The top text 'when the americans pull up outside of auschwitz' is juxtaposed with the visual of Nazi leaders (including Adolf Hitler) standing before swastika flags. This creates an analogical mapping where the historical event of American forces arriving at Auschwitz (a moment of liberation and the end of Nazi atrocities) is visually represented by the image of the Nazi regime's leaders. The mapping implies that the visual material (Nazi leaders) represents the 'before' state of the event described in the text (American arrival), thereby establishing a direct visual-textual correspondence.",
